c generated tseitin-torus-3x3-odd
c Tseitin formula over a 4-regular 3x3 toroidal grid, unsatisfiable.
c Emitted by tseitin_torus_case of [3, 3, 1] in lib/bench.eigs -- regenerate
c with that call rather than editing this file by hand.
c One variable per torus edge (18 edges: h(r,c)=r*3+c+1, v(r,c)=9+r*3+c+1).
c Each vertex constrains the XOR of its four incident edges to its charge;
c vertex (0,0) carries charge 1 and the rest 0, so the total charge is odd
c and the formula is UNSAT. Resolution refutations of Tseitin formulas need
c size exponential in the graph's expansion (Urquhart 1987) -- this is the
c parity/expansion hard family, distinct from pigeonhole's counting hardness.
p cnf 18 72
